WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.030
Here's how to aim with gyro and Flick Stick in PadForge.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.110
You're hearing a generated voice.

3
00:00:07.525 --> 00:00:10.065
This Keyboard + Mouse controller has a DualSense assigned.

4
00:00:10.105 --> 00:00:13.335
Open it, and go to the Gyro tab.

5
00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.860
Put the controller down, hands off, and click Calibrate Gyro.

6
00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:21.360
The live readout should then sit near zero.

7
00:00:22.735 --> 00:00:27.285
Below it, Sensitivity sets how far the pointer moves for each turn of the pad.

8
00:00:28.604 --> 00:00:32.774
On the Mappings tab, click the Mouse X row, and open its source list.

9
00:00:34.447 --> 00:00:37.597
Scroll to Flick Stick, for the right stick, and pick it.

10
00:00:39.328 --> 00:00:42.218
Then click the Mouse Y row, and open its list.

11
00:00:43.503 --> 00:00:47.813
Gyro Pitch sits right after the touchpad inputs, near the end of the list.

12
00:00:48.283 --> 00:00:48.773
Pick it.

13
00:00:49.953 --> 00:00:54.343
Now the stick turns you left and right, and tilting the pad aims up and down.

14
00:00:55.674 --> 00:00:58.704
On the Sticks tab, scroll to the end of the page.

15
00:00:59.434 --> 00:01:01.244
Flick Stick has a card of its own there,

16
00:01:01.414 --> 00:01:03.884
and its Flick Time sets how long a turn takes.

17
00:01:05.174 --> 00:01:07.844
Nothing moves while the pad sits on the desk.

18
00:01:08.314 --> 00:01:12.044
Pick it up, flick the right stick to turn, and tilt the pad to aim.

19
00:01:14.408 --> 00:01:16.938
Find more guides at padforge.org.
